,title,link,text,language,family
0,Margi language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margi_language,"May 28, 2026 - Margi, also known as Marghi and Marghi Central, is a Chadic language (a branch of Afroasiatic) spoken in Nigeria, Cameroon, and Chad. It is perhaps the best described of the Biu–Mandara branch of that family.",Marghi Central,Afro-Asiatic
1,Biu–Mandara languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biu–Mandara_languages,"The Biu–Mandara or Central Chadic languages of the Afro-Asiatic family are spoken in Nigeria, Chad and Cameroon. A reconstruction of Proto-Central Chadic has been proposed by Gravina (2014).",Marghi Central,Afro-Asiatic
2,Marghi people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marghi_people,"January 27, 2026 - As a result of their settlement in diverse areas, the Marghi people were exposed to various cultural influences from neighboring ethnic groups, such as the Kamwe people, which they scornfully called higi in 1937 Kanuri, Kilba, and Pabir (Babur). The Margi, Kamwe, Bura and Chibok people are a branch of the Afro-Asiatic ...",Marghi Central,Afro-Asiatic
3,Music of Asia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Asia,"May 23, 2026 - Asian music encompasses numerous musical styles, diverse cultural and religious traditions, and forms originating on the Asian continent. ... Wikimedia Commons has media related to Asian music.",Marghi Central,Afro-Asiatic
4,Sounding the Indian Ocean: Musical Circulations in the Afro ...,https://shc.stanford.edu/arcade/interventions/sounding-indian-ocean-musical-circulations-afro-asiatic-seascape-introduction,"It situates Abu Dhabi, Dubai, and Singapore—each now among the world’s premier metropolises—as central to Indian Ocean music studies. Such cities emerge in the volume as key urban nodes with others of historic importance (e.g., Cape Town, Zanzibar, Colombo, Penang).",Marghi Central,Afro-Asiatic
